From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Lopez <norelec@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:04:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Macros: a Loop option

A macro flagged as looping restarts from its first action when it ends, until
its hotkey is pressed again or ESC stops it. Rewinding happens once per frame
with a 250ms floor, so a macro without a Delay cannot lock the client up or
flood the server, and keyboard auto-repeat does not toggle it. The macro button
turns green while the loop runs, and the flag is saved in macros.xml.

The code lives in MacroManager.Loop.cs and MacroControl.Distro.cs, the
"Loop (ESC to stop)" text in Resources/ResDistro.resx; upstream's files only
carry the calls into them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LFcBNQtF3Z7vfzi99BXwUe
